# Workspaces and layout

Paneform keeps a model of connected displays, workspaces, and windows. Commands act on this model and the layout engine applies the resulting positions.

## Workspaces

A workspace groups windows. The focused workspace is the one you are viewing. Use `wm workspace focus <workspace>` to change it; a new name can be created on first use.

## Tiling and floating

In BSP mode, windows share the available area. Floating windows remain in their workspace but are excluded from automatic tiling. Use the [command reference](/wm/docs/commands/) to see the exact forms.

## Pausing

Pause holds automatic mutations. Resume to let the manager reconcile the desktop again.
